lass="wprm-recipe-jump wprm-recipe-link wprm-jump-to-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-jump-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent">Jump to Recipe</a>

<a href="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wprm_print/greek-chicken-marinade" style="color: #ffffff;background-color: #14452f;border-color: #18392b;border-radius: 3px;padding: 5px 8px;" class="wprm-recipe-print wprm-recipe-link wprm-print-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-print-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent" data-recipe-id="1442" data-template="" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">Print Recipe</a></div></div></div></div><div class="site-inner"><div class="content-sidebar-wrap"><main class="content" id="genesis-content"><article class="post-1440 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail category-main-dish category-recipes entry" aria-label="The Best Greek Chicken Marinade with Lemon and Dill"><div class="entry-content"><div class="tasty-links-general-disclaimer"><p>This post contains affiliate links.</p>
</div>

<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="isPasted">Grilled Greek chicken is a quick, healthy, and easy dish I know you'll love. With a marinade that combines the fresh, vibrant flavors of lemon, dill, and fresh garlic, this flavorful chicken&nbsp;will transport your taste buds straight to the Mediterranean. In this post, you'll find tips for marinading and grilling so you can make the most tender, delicious grilled Greek-style chicken possible! Let's get started!</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" fetchpriority="high" src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-5.jpg" alt="a platter with grilled chicken, sliced lemons and dill. Some of the chicken is cut into pieces and some of it is whole." data-skip-lazy class="wp-image-5081" srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-5.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-5-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-5-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-5-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-5-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-5-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-5-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Greek food is hands down my favorite food. I love the classic Greek flavors of lemon, dill and garlic...mmmmm...sign me up! I created this simple Mediterranean-inspired marinade one afternoon while craving those 3 awesome flavors. It only involves a few simple ingredients, and proves you don't need a lot of ingredients to get a big amount of flavor. It is now one of my go-to chicken recipes.&nbsp;</p>


<style></style><details id="feast-advanced-jump-to"open><summary>Jump to:</summary><ul id="feast-jump-to-list"><li><a href="#ingredients">Ingredients</a></li><li><a href="#instructions">Instructions</a></li><li><a href="#marinating-tips">Marinating Tips</a></li><li><a href="#grilling-tips">Grilling Tips</a></li><li><a href="#serving-suggestions">Serving Suggestions</a></li><li><a href="#variations">Variations</a></li><li><a href="#equipment">Equipment</a></li><li><a href="#faq-and-troubleshooting">FAQ and Troubleshooting</a></li><li><a href="#conclusion">Conclusion</a></li><li><a href="#h-recipe">Recipe</a></li><li><a href="#comments">Reviews</a></li></ul></details>


<h2 id="ingredients"   class="wp-block-heading">Ingredients</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">For the Lemon Dill Marinade:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>extra virgin olive oil</li>



<li>fresh lemon juice</li>



<li>garlic cloves</li>



<li>fresh or dried dill</li>



<li>salt and black pepper</li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">For the Grilled Chicken:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts (or any preferred cut of chicken, such as chicken thighs)</li>
</ul>



<h2 id="instructions"   class="wp-block-heading">Instructions</h2>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-7387b849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201798'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="a bowl of greek chicken marinade. Garlic, dill and lemons are next to the bowl." class="wp-image-5078" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2.jpg" alt="a bowl of greek chicken marinade. Garlic, dill and lemons are next to the bowl." class="wp-image-5078" srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-2-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>1. Prepare the Greek Marinade Ingredients</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In a medium-sized bowl, combine all of the Greek marinade ingredients.  Whisk these ingredients together until well combined.</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201798'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="chicken breasts marinating with lemon slices, dill and garlic." class="wp-image-5079" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3.jpg" alt="chicken breasts marinating with lemon slices, dill and garlic." class="wp-image-5079" srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-3-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>2. Marinate the Chicken</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Place the chicken breasts in a shallow dish. Pour the Greek-style marinade over the chicken, ensuring each piece is well coated. Cover the dish and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes. For the best flavor, marinate the chicken for 2-4 hours.</p>
</div>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-style-group-lightbulb"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<h2 id="marinating-tips"   class="wp-block-heading">Marinating Tips</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Here are some helpful tips for marinating this lemony Greek chicken to ensure it turns out flavorful and tender.</p>



<ol class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Use Fresh Ingredients</strong>: Opt for fresh herbs, garlic, and lemon juice when possible. Fresh ingredients have more vibrant flavors compared to dried or bottled alternatives.</li>



<li><strong>Balance the Flavors</strong>: &nbsp;A good marinade typically includes acid (like lemon juice or vinegar), fat (like olive oil), and seasonings (like herbs, spices, garlic). The acid helps tenderize the meat, the fat adds moisture and richness, and the seasonings provide depth of flavor.</li>



<li><strong>Proper Marinating Time</strong>: &nbsp;Marinate the chicken for at least 30 minutes to let the flavors penetrate. For more intense flavor, marinate for 2-4 hours. Overnight marination is ideal but be cautious not to exceed 24 hours as the acid can start to break down the meat too much, making it mushy.</li>



<li><strong>Use a Non-reactive Container</strong>: &nbsp;Always use glass, ceramic, or food-grade plastic containers for marinating. Avoid metal containers as they can react with acidic ingredients and alter the marinade's flavor.</li>



<li><strong>Ensure Even Coating</strong>: &nbsp;Turn the chicken occasionally while it's marinating to ensure all pieces are evenly coated. You can also massage the marinade into the outside of the chicken to help it absorb better.</li>



<li><strong>Refrigerate While Marinating</strong>: &nbsp;Always marinate Greek chicken in an airtight container refrigerator to prevent bacterial growth. Do not leave chicken out at room temperature for extended periods.</li>
</ol>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-7387b849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201798'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="chicken breasts on a grill." class="wp-image-5080" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4.jpg" alt="chicken breasts on a grill." class="wp-image-5080" srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-4-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>3. Grill the Chicken</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="isPasted">While the chicken is marinating to Grecian perfection, preheat your outdoor grill to&nbsp;<strong>medium-high heat</strong>. If you're using a charcoal grill, prepare the coals until they're covered with white ash. For a gas grill, preheat for about 10 minutes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Once the grill is ready, remove the chicken from the Mediterranean marinade and place the chicken breasts on the grill. Cook on medium heat for 6-7 minutes on each side, or until the internal temperature reaches 165°F (75°C). Cooking time will vary based on how thick your chicken breasts are. The chicken should be golden brown with a slightly charred exterior.</p>



<div class="wp-block-group is-style-group-lightbulb"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<h2 id="grilling-tips"   class="wp-block-heading">Grilling Tips</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Grilling chicken breasts can be tricky because they can easily dry out if not cooked properly. Here are some tips to ensure your grilled chicken breasts turn out juicy and flavorful every time:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">1.&nbsp;<strong>Choose Uniform Breasts</strong>: &nbsp;Select chicken breasts of similar size and thickness to ensure even cooking. If they are uneven, pound them to an even thickness using a meat mallet.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>2. &nbsp;Preheat the Grill:&nbsp;</strong>Preheat your grill to medium-high heat (about 375-450°F or 190-232°C) before placing the chicken on it. This ensures that the chicken cooks evenly and develops a good sear.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>3. &nbsp;Oil the Grill Grates:&nbsp;</strong>To prevent the chicken from sticking, oil the grill grates before cooking. Use a paper towel dipped in oil and tongs to rub the grates.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>4. Avoid Overcrowding:&nbsp;</strong>Leave space between each piece of chicken on the grill. This allows for even cooking and prevents steaming.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">5.&nbsp;<strong>Flip Only Once: &nbsp;</strong>Flip the chicken breasts only once during grilling. Constant flipping can cause the chicken to lose moisture and not develop a proper crust.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">6. &nbsp;<strong>Use a Meat Thermometer:&nbsp;</strong>Use an instant-read thermometer to check the internal temperature. The chicken is done when it reaches 165°F (75°C) in the thickest part of the meat. This ensures it's safe to eat without being overcooked. &nbsp;Overcooking chicken breasts is the #1 reason they turn out rubbery and tough. &nbsp;</p>
</div></div>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201798'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="a platter of grilled chicken, sliced lemons and dill." class="wp-image-5082" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1798" src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6.jpg" alt="a platter of grilled chicken, sliced lemons and dill." class="wp-image-5082" srcset="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6.jpg 1200w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-360x539.jpg 360w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-720x1079.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-1025x1536.jpg 1025w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-180x270.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/greek-chicken-marinade-6-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>5. Rest and Serve</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After grilling, let the Greek chicken breasts rest for 5 minutes. This allows the juices to be redistributed, ensuring the meat is moist and tender.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now your grilled Greek chicken is ready to be enjoyed! &nbsp;Let's find out how to serve it!</p>
</div>
</div>



<h2 id="serving-suggestions"   class="wp-block-heading">Serving Suggestions</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="isPasted">This lemon and dill-flavored chicken can be served in so many ways!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One of my favorite ways to serve this dill chicken is over a green salad with feta cheese and a&nbsp;<a href="https://www.littlebroken.com/greek-vinaigrette/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Greek vinaigrette</a>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It's also perfect for Greek chicken gyros! Just wrap it up in a pita with lettuce, onions, tomatoes, cucumbers, and feta cheese. Don't forget to dip it in&nbsp;<a href="https://www.loveandlemons.com/tzatziki-sauce/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Tzatziki sauce</a>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Here are some other great recipes that would go perfectly with this Lemony garlic chicken:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.cookingclassy.com/greek-salad/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Cucumber and Tomato Greek Salad</a></li>



<li><a href="https://tastykitchen.com/recipes/breads/soft-fluffy-whole-wheat-pita-bread/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Soft and Fluffy Whole Wheat Pita Bread</a></li>
</ul>


