ads/2020/08/2_jars_pickled_carrots_2-640x853.jpg 640w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/2_jars_pickled_carrots_2-720x960.jpg 720w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/2_jars_pickled_carrots_2-180x240.jpg 180w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/2_jars_pickled_carrots_2-17x24.jpg 17w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/2_jars_pickled_carrots_2-26x36.jpg 26w, https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/2_jars_pickled_carrots_2-35x48.jpg 35w" sizes="(max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" /></noscript><div class="fsri-title">Pickled Carrots with Lemon and Garlic</div></a></li></ul></div>


<h2 id="variations"   class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Variations</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There are several delicious customizations you can make to this quick and easy chicken marinade.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Alternative fresh herbs: mint, parsley, oregano or basil.</li>



<li>Add a tablespoon of honey for a sweet and tangy flavor.</li>



<li>Add in lemon zest to really bring out the lemon flavor.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This lemon and dill Greek marinade can also be used for other types of meat. &nbsp;Try it out on:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>lamb</li>



<li>fish</li>



<li>tofu</li>



<li>beef</li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Greek Chicken Kabobs</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This easy marinade is also perfect for making kabobs, also known as chicken souvlaki. &nbsp;Simply cut your raw chicken into large chunks and skewer them on wooden skewers before marinating them.&nbsp;</p>



<h2 id="equipment"   class="wp-block-heading">Equipment</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Here are a few tools that I find vital when making this greek chicken marinade.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Instant-Read <a href="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-admin/post.php?post=5069&amp;action=edit">Digital Meat Thermometer</a>:  If you want to make the best grilled chicken possible, you HAVE to be able to take the temperature of the meat while it's cooking.  </li>



<li>I love these <a href="https://amzn.to/3VDNWq6">longer grill tongs</a> so I don't burn my arms while grilling.</li>



<li>I've tried to cut back on my single-use plastic consumption.  I love using this <a href="https://amzn.to/3VDOwnM">marinade container</a> instead of ziplock bags.  </li>
</ul>



