<h2 id="faq-and-troubleshooting"   class="wp-block-heading">FAQ and Troubleshooting</h2>



<div class="schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block"><div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1719356794686"><strong class="schema-faq-question">How long should I marinate the chicken?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">I recommend marinating your chicken for 2-4 hours.  However, if you are pinched for time, aim for at least 20 minutes.  <br/><br/>I don't recommend marinating your chicken longer than 24 hours because the acid in the lemon juice can start to break down the meat and make it mushy.  </p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1719356810921"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Can I freeze the marinated chicken?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Yes!  I recommend placing the raw chicken and the marinade in a reusable ziplock bag and laying it flat in the freezer.  When you are ready to use, thaw overnight in the refrigerator for best results.  </p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1719356826789"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Why did my chicken turn out dry or rubbery?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">That is usually because the chicken was overcooked.  I highly recommend using an instant-read meat thermometer to check the internal temperature. The chicken is done when it reaches 165°F (75°C) in the thickest part. If you cook it longer than that it will get tougher and chewier.  </p> </div> </div>



<h2 id="conclusion"   class="wp-block-heading">Conclusion</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Grilled Greek chicken is a flavorful, healthy dish that's easy to prepare and sure to be a hit. With the tangy lemon, aromatic garlic, and fresh dill, this marinade creates a delicious and tender chicken that's perfect for any occasion. Try this recipe for your next meal and enjoy a Mediterranean vibe right at home!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Feel free to leave a comment below with your favorite Greek dishes or any variations you've tried with this recipe. I'm always looking for more Greek recipes. &nbsp;It is my favorite genre of food!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">✌️Ems</p>


