			<p class="comment-meta"><time class="comment-time">July 02, 2020 at 4:47 pm</time></p>		</header>

		<div class="comment-content">
			
			<p><img class="wprm-comment-rating" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODdhAQABAPAAAP///wAAACwAAAAAAQABAEACAkQBADs=" data-lazy-src="https://www.theincrediblebulks.com/wp-content/plugins/wp-recipe-maker/assets/icons/rating/stars-alt-5.svg" alt="5 stars" width="80" height="16" /><br />
This chicken is amazing! All my kids are it without asking for a dip... Haha. We'll definitely be making this a lot!</p>
		</div>

		<div class="comment-reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-552" data-commentid="552" data-postid="1440" data-belowelement="article-comment-552" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Jennifer Lund" aria-label="Reply to Jennifer Lund">Reply</a></div>
		
	</article>
	</li><!-- #comment-## -->

	<li class="comment odd alt thread-odd thread-alt depth-1" id="comment-1638">
	<article id="article-comment-1638">

		
		<header class="comment-header">
			<p class="comment-author">
				<span class="comment-author-name">K</span>			</p>

			<p class="comment-meta"><time class="comment-time">July 25, 2024 at 8:04 am</time></p>		</header>

		<div class="comment-content">
			
			<p>I've done many similar marinades for chicken breast in the past. I was curious as to why there was no salt in this recipe. So I added a tsp of salt. Big mistake! The chicken lost most of its liquids when I took it out of the marinade after a couple hours. Sadly it was pretty dry when it was done.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="comment-reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-1638" data-commentid="1638" data-postid="1440" data-belowelement="article-comment-1638" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to K" aria-label="Reply to K">Reply</a></div>
		
	</article>
	</li><!-- #comment-## -->

	<li class="comment even thread-even depth-1" id="comment-1872">
